# Ogg's modular unit lies in the full level-N function field

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionFieldFull`
(`55ba7334-be8a-5179-a36e-7862c943490d`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `bbb00a88-70a0-5648-8976-119669fb911b`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $\Delta =$
[`ModularCurve.deltaSeries`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L107) for the Laurent series over
$\mathbb{Q}$ given by $q$ (the Hahn series $q^{1}$ with coefficient $1$) times the power series
`dedekindEtaUnitQ`, and for $d \ge 1$ let `qExpand ℚ d` denote the substitution $q \mapsto q^{d}$ on
`LaurentSeries ℚ`. The theorem asserts that the element
[`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries N`](def/ModularCurve_ModularUnit.html#L127) $= \Delta(q)\cdot
\Delta(q^{N})^{-1}$, the product of $\Delta$ with the inverse of its $N$-th $q$-expansion
`deltaSeriesN N`, belongs to [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull
N`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L305), namely the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries ℚ` over
$\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of all series $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q},d}(\mathtt{jq})$ for
nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, i.e. by the $q$-expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid N$. No primality or
other hypothesis on $N$ is imposed: the assertion is unconditional in the level.

This is the statement that Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(q)/\Delta(q^{N})$ is a rational function of
the expansions $j(q^{d})$, $d \mid N$, at arbitrary, not merely prime, level; in the formalisation
it supplies the unit used to produce functions with prescribed divisors on the modular curve of
level $N$. It is cited throughout the construction of Deligne–Rapoport-style models and charts at
general level.

